# nix-f: f folds Nix (#1351). On a let's first line f folds the let to the end of its body and f
# there unfolds it; inside an attribute set f folds that set. The file is written here, not in
# the project, which every other scenario counts the files of.
merl
wait Open a file (fuzzy)
run mkdir -p nix && printf '{ pkgs, ... }:\n\nlet\n  name = "merl";\nin\n{\n  environment.systemPackages = [\n    pkgs.git\n  ];\n  users.users.merl = {\n    home = "/Users/merl";\n  };\n}\n' > nix/default.nix
key q
wait merl exited: 0
merl nix/default.nix
wait A default.nix
key :
type 3
key Enter f
wait 9 lines ⋯ }
key f :
type 11
key Enter f
wait 1 line ⋯ };
key q
wait merl exited: 0
